<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Ireland's Ryanair joins Irish/US stock markets.</title>
<headline>Ireland's Ryanair joins Irish/US stock markets.</headline>
<byline>Carmel Linnane</byline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ireland's 'low-budget' airline Ryanair announced on Tuesday it wanted to float on the Irish stock exchange and the Nasdaq in the United States, the first Irish company to seek a simultaneous quote on both sides of the Atlantic.</p>
<p>Ryanair is offering approximately 54.2 million shares at between 165 Irish pence ($2.46) and 195 Irish pence for a market capitalisation of 261.2 million Irish pounds ($389.4 million) to 308.7 million Irish pounds.</p>
</text>
